*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.backup
.env.production
# Any hand-made copy of .env holds the same keys the real one does. The three
# patterns above are Laravel's defaults and none of them catches .env.bak,
# .env.old, or .env.2026-09-06 — the names somebody actually types before
# editing a live file. A leaked key is not undone by deleting the file after.
.env.*
!.env.example
.phpactor.json
.phpunit.result.cache
/.fleet
/.idea
/.nova
/.phpunit.cache
/.vscode
/.zed
/auth.json
/database/database.sqlite
/node_modules
/public/hot
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/vendor
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
Thumbs.db

# Debris from `curl` testing against the local site. Both hold real
# credentials — a `primepower-session` cookie and an `XSRF-TOKEN` — and three
# of these were sitting untracked in the working tree waiting to be committed
# to a public repository. Ignored by name rather than trusted to be cleaned up.
cookies.txt
/storage/cookies.txt
/storage/*response*.html
